    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "$\\frac{3}{7}$ of a sum of money is $\\$21$. How much is $\\frac{4}{5}$ of the sum of money?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$39.20$",
      "worked": "One-seventh of the sum is $\\$21\\div3=\\$7$.\nThe whole sum is $7\\times\\$7=\\$49$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{4}{5}\\times49&=4\\times\\frac{49}{5}\\\\\\frac{4}{5}\\times49&=\\frac{196}{5}\\\\\\frac{4}{5}\\times49&=39.2\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, four-fifths of the sum is $\\$39.20$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
